<title>NETHERLANDS: SECOND DUTCH SUGAR BEET YIELD AT 9.6 TONNES.</title>
<headline>SECOND DUTCH SUGAR BEET YIELD AT 9.6 TONNES.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The second Dutch sugar beet forecast for 1997 showed a yield of 9.6 tonnes per hectare white value, up from 9.3 tonnes in 1996, the Institute for Sugar Research (IRS) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>IRS also said beet weight per hectare was forecast at 60.1 tonnes against an average 1996 weight of 56.00 and an annual average between 1987 and 1996 of 58.7 tonnes.</p>
<p>This is the second of the computer-generated forecasts to be issued this season. Instigated last year, the estimates replace traditional forecasts based on crop reports from the field.</p>
<p>The next forecast will be made on August 27, IRS said.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
